WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.840 align:middle line:90%

2
00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.730 align:middle line:84%
So one of my clients
just called and asked

3
00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.740 align:middle line:84%
for a quick working lunch
to go over their project.

4
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.670 align:middle line:84%
Now I'm going to add it to the
calendar so I won't forget.

5
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.530 align:middle line:84%
Let's click on the date
and name it "Client Lunch."

6
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.970 align:middle line:84%
It's at 11 AM and it can
stay as an event rather than

7
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.379 align:middle line:90%
a milestone.

8
00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:19.493 align:middle line:84%
Click Add This Event and
it's on the calendar.

9
00:00:19.493 --> 00:00:20.910 align:middle line:84%
But what if the
client called back

10
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.010 align:middle line:90%
to push it to the next day?

11
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.740 align:middle line:84%
I'm going to click on the
event, change the date,

12
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.970 align:middle line:90%
and click Save.

13
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.500 align:middle line:84%
The event's now moved
to the new time.

14
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.000 align:middle line:90%
